// Aggregate-free sibling of 0179 (`count … > 0`). "At least one Login in
// the window" needs no aggregation: `count for (t). where (formerly … Login
// && tp(t)) > 0` is equivalent to a bare positive existence of a Login in
// the window. Exercises `exists` restricting a data variable by a predicate
// field (rather than by an aggregate equality). Verdicts must match 0179.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (u: String). formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: u, input.server: context.input.server }};
